        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "1.) An employee on approved Family Illness Leave may elect to use accrued compensatory time off in accordance with Article 12 - Hours of Work prior to beginning FMLA leave. An employee may, at the discretion of the University, elect to use accrued vacation time before taking a FMLA leave without pay. If the employee's vacation leave accrual is at maximum the employee will be required to use at least 10% of the vacation leave credit prior to taking leave without pay. Up to five (5) days of accrued sick leave per year may be substituted for Family Illness Leave granted under this section pursuant to Article 36 - Sick Leave, Section B.3.b.",
            "block_bbox": [
